Game and engine (engine/)
  Critical Mass (Critter), Copyright (C) 2001-2024 Frank Becker.
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (engine/COPYING).
  Debian's copyright file for the game (criticalmass, in main) lists all of it,
  code and data, under the same license.
  Source: https://github.com/mooflu/critter, commit
  c4c0b4df13079e8ec64ed5e5ac767b0cdd5bf39c, with frunk.store's changes for this
  site in engine/critter-web.patch (also tools/critter/critter-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-critter.mjs
  builds it). The source the build came from is
  engine/critter-c4c0b4df1307-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: the page mounts the saves and sets the drawing size; the game
  no longer grabs the pointer on its own; web_* functions let the page pass on
  touch and controllers and ask for saves; a longer sound buffer; no Quit,
  Fullscreen or Resolution items in the menu; the top-ten name comes from the
  page; no quick-exit key.

Music
  The soundtrack upstream ships ("Critical: Lunar Gravity's Millennium Remake")
  has no license and is left out. In its place, data/music/overdrive.ogg is
  "Overdrive" by Centurion_of_war, CC0, from
  https://opengameart.org/content/overdrive

